---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ArticleCard from '../../components/article/ArticleCard.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Vipul Otari, Publisher & Research Editor"
  description="Meet Vipul Otari, publisher and research editor of HomeGeneratorGuide. See the publication’s research method, scope, and review limitations."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }, { href: '/about/', label: 'About' }, { label: 'Vipul Otari' }]} />
    <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-4">
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="flex h-16 w-16 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary text-2xl font-bold text-white">V</span>
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-primary">Vipul Otari</h1>
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-600">Publisher & Research Editor, HomeGeneratorGuide</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-hgg mt-6">
      <h2>Editorial role and limits</h2>
      <p>Vipul Otari is identified here as the publisher and research editor for HomeGeneratorGuide. The site’s work is desk research: reviewing public manufacturer documentation, government material, safety guidance, and clearly labeled estimates, then explaining where those sources do and do not answer a homeowner’s question.</p>
      <p>This role is not a trade credential. The publisher is not presented as a licensed electrician, electrical engineer, generator installer, or product tester. The site does not claim in-person installation experience, hands-on equipment testing, or independent reliability testing. Its articles are educational research and cannot replace an on-site load calculation, equipment-specific instructions, or local code review.</p>
      <h2>Research standards</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Prefer current manufacturer pages, specification sheets, operator manuals, government sources, and recognized safety authorities.</li>
        <li>Label manufacturer statements as manufacturer-published information; distinguish estimates from measured or model-specific facts.</li>
        <li>Omit values that cannot be verified rather than filling gaps from a different model, fuel, or reseller listing.</li>
        <li>Do not sell generator or installer leads, and do not accept payment for rankings or conclusions.</li>
        <li>For corrections, <a href="/contact/">send the page URL and source</a>; material changes should be documented on the page.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>See the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> for details about source checks and corrections, and the <a href="/review-process/">professional review status</a> for current review limitations.</p>
      <h2>Start reading</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <ArticleCard href="/sizing/what-size-generator-do-i-need/" title="What Size Generator Do I Need?" description="A load-first process and static worksheet." category="Sizing" />
      <ArticleCard href="/cost/standby-generator-cost/" title="Standby Generator Cost Guide" description="Understand estimates, project scope, and written quotes." category="Cost" />
    </div>
    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-gray-600">Site method: <a href="/about/" class="underline decoration-accent underline-offset-4">About</a> · <a href="/editorial-policy/" class="underline decoration-accent underline-offset-4">Editorial Policy</a> · <a href="/disclaimer/" class="underline decoration-accent underline-offset-4">Disclaimer</a></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
